From aa3bf51c9dec12cf55ca2e7e8f3e38e07a55baf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:32:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: let the left ring slot try every ring in the best-gear
 search

borg_best_stuff_aux() picks the best combination of equipment at home
by trying each candidate item in each slot, the left ring slot before
the right one (see borg_best_stuff_order()).  To avoid putting the same
ring on both hands, the right-slot loop skips the item already chosen
for the left slot, which is correct.

The left-slot loop also had such a check, against test[n + 1], the
right-slot entry.  The right slot has not been chosen yet at that
point: the entry still holds the last ring tried for the right slot in
the previous subtree.  So a ring was skipped for the left slot whenever
it was the last ring tried on the right.  With one ring in the pack,
the search never tried it on the left hand.  A Borg wearing a weak
left ring and a good right ring then planned to take off the good ring
to make room for the new one, keeping the weak ring.

The right-slot check already prevents duplicates, so drop the left-slot
one.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#86.
---
 src/borg/borg-item-wear.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c b/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
index 9464197d1..9d697346a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-item-wear.c
@@ -1283,19 +1283,14 @@ static void borg_best_stuff_aux(
                     && borg_wield_slot(item) == INVEN_LEFT)))
             continue;
 
-        /* don't test the same item in both ring slots */
+        /* don't test the same item in both ring slots; the left ring is
+         * chosen first, so only the right ring needs the check */
         if (slot == INVEN_RIGHT) {
             if (i < z_info->pack_size) {
                 if (test[n - 1] == i)
                     continue;
             } else if (test[n - 1] == ((i - z_info->pack_size) + 100))
                 continue;
-        } else if (slot == INVEN_LEFT) {
-            if (i < z_info->pack_size) {
-                if (test[n + 1] == i)
-                    continue;
-            } else if (test[n + 1] == ((i - z_info->pack_size) + 100))
-                continue;
         }
 
         /* Make sure that slot does not have an item that can't be removed */
